      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1248223970,
      "text": "Peltophorum africanum, the weeping wattle, is a semi-deciduous to deciduous flowering tree growing to about 15 meters tall. It is native to Africa south of the equator. Their yellow flowers bloom on the ends of branches in upright, showy sprays."
    },
